    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d784-a1">

                <pb facs="0640" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg524"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-04T18:25:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1914, 6.25 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Since our telegram of this morning we have been reading Oppenheim and Moore as to
                    the office of mediation and though they indicate that it is a governmental act
                    they furnish no suggestion as to how far the Mediators can be directed by their
                    Governments. Mr. Lehmann is of the opinion that, the mediation being a
                    governmental function, the Mediators may properly maintain themselves in harmony
                    with the views of their Governments and may properly consult their Governments.
                    Judge Lamar takes a different view, unless their countries are parties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Commissioners</hi>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
